 "text": "Hey, how are you doing? It depends on you, the weather, and how hot it is. A good rule of thumb is one hundred millilitres per hour. small bottle on the handlebars can help you drink without stopping. If you do stop, get a glass that people at the top won't steal. A bar every two hours is about right. Full energy gels every hour if you need the fast energy. Fill up on water at stops. You can, but few people do. A empty stomach feels much less empty an hour after waking up.",
